        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "18-3-3 The maximum secondary load, the number of students for which a teacher shall be responsible for evaluating, will be 150 students per day for each classroom teacher. To exceed the one hundred fifty (150) maximum, the principal will collaborate with the affected teacher to insure that course objectives and standards can be met with the additional students. The principal and the teacher will attempt to arrive at a mutually agreeable decision. If they cannot do that the curriculum specialist in the affected content area will provide consultation. Laboratory classes shall not exceed the number of students which can be safely taught at the number of work stations in the classroom.",
            "block_bbox": [
